# Security headers for every response. Put this file at public/_headers so the
# build copies it into dist/ and the prebuilt upload carries it.
# Standard: https://qiheme.github.io/handbook/#/standards/frontend-checklist
#
# These cover the Front-End Checklist's header rules: HSTS, X-Frame-Options,
# X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy and Permissions-Policy.
#
# A Content-Security-Policy is required too, but it is specific to each app: it
# must list the app's own API and font hosts. Add the line below to the block,
# watch the browser console on a preview deploy, then rename the header to
# Content-Security-Policy once nothing is reported.
#
#   Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; style-src 'self' https://fonts.googleapis.com; img-src 'self' data:; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
#
# The two rules at the bottom let browsers keep fingerprinted build files for a
# year: Vite writes them to /assets/, Astro to /_astro/. Their names change
# whenever their content does, so they are safe to cache forever.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
